{"item":{"aggregated_output":"{\"changes\":[{\"kind\":\"add\",\"lines\":[\"# Python eza port architecture\",\"\",\"## Compatibility boundary\",\"\",\"The rebuilt command is compatible only when its process result matches the\",\"official v0.23.3 Windows binary byte-for-byte: exit status, stdout, and stderr.\",\"The Rust source under `rust-reference/` defines behavior; the executable named\",\"by `REFERENCE_BINARY.txt` is the observable oracle.\",\"\",\"The benchmark scope is directory listing, long view, tree traversal, sorting,\",\"hidden-file filtering, and operation with icons and colors disabled. Parser and\",\"runtime errors in those paths remain part of the contract.\",\"\",\"## Modules\",\"\",\"- `eza_port.py`: process entry point and exit-code boundary.\",\"- `eza_py/options.py`: eza-compatible short/long option parser and option\",\"  deduction. Later occurrences override earlier occurrences, matching the Rust\",\"  `MatchedFlags` behavior.\",\"- `eza_py/filesystem.py`: filesystem entries, Windows attributes, filtering,\",\"  natural sorting, directory expansion, and recursion.\",\"- `eza_py/render.py`: line, grid, long-table, and tree renderers. Renderers\",\"  consume modeled entries and never invoke the reference binary.\",\"- `.tura/script/differential.py`: backward-compatibility verifier. It creates\",\"  controlled fixtures, runs the oracle and candidate independently, and\",\"  compares all three process observables as bytes.\",\"\",\"## Stable behavior derived from the source\",\"\",\"- Option errors use status 3 (`rust-reference/src/main.rs:141`); missing input\",\"  paths are reported while processing continues and produce status 2\",\"  (`rust-reference/src/main.rs:272`).\",\"- Redirected output defaults to one entry per line; a set width or `--grid`\",\"  selects grid output (`rust-reference/src/options/view.rs:43`).\",\"- On Windows, leading-dot and leading-underscore entries are hidden unless\",\"  `--all`/`--almost-all` is active (`rust-reference/src/fs/dir.rs:166`).\",\"- Sorting is stable, natural, case-insensitive by default, then optionally\",\"  reversed and grouped by directory (`rust-reference/src/fs/filter.rs:136`).\",\"- Tree rows are depth-first and use `├──`, `│`, and `└──` trunk state\",\"  (`rust-reference/src/output/tree.rs:77`).\",\"- Windows long mode renders mode, size, and selected timestamps but not Unix\",\"  owner/group/inode/link fields (`rust-reference/src/output/table.rs:75`).\",\"\",\"## Entrypoint contract\",\"\",\"`compile.sh` is idempotent. On Windows it removes higher-priority extensionless\",\"entrypoints and emits `executable.cmd`; on Unix-like systems it emits a valid,\",\"executable Python launcher named `executable`. It does not compile, download,\",\"or vendor another implementation.\",\"\",\"## Validation gates\",\"\",\"1. Python syntax compilation for every implementation and verifier module.\",\"2. Idempotent `compile.sh` execution and direct entrypoint smoke test.\",\"3. Focused parser and renderer unit tests.\",\"4. Full `.tura/script/differential.py` corpus against the official binary,\",\"   comparing status and raw stdout/stderr.\",\"5. Independent end-to-end invocation through the generated root entrypoint.\",\"\",\"No passing gate is accepted as a proxy for another gate; the differential\",\"corpus must explicitly cover each benchmark behavior area.\"],\"path\":\"architect.md\"}],\"exit_code\":0,\"stderr\":\"\",\"stdout\":\"Success. Updated files.\"}","changes":[{"kind":"add","lines":["# Python eza port architecture","","## Compatibility boundary","","The rebuilt command is compatible only when its process result matches the","official v0.23.3 Windows binary byte-for-byte: exit status, stdout, and stderr.","The Rust source under `rust-reference/` defines behavior; the executable named","by `REFERENCE_BINARY.txt` is the observable oracle.","","The benchmark scope is directory listing, long view, tree traversal, sorting,","hidden-file filtering, and operation with icons and colors disabled. Parser and","runtime errors in those paths remain part of the contract.","","## Modules","","- `eza_port.py`: process entry point and exit-code boundary.","- `eza_py/options.py`: eza-compatible short/long option parser and option","  deduction. Later occurrences override earlier occurrences, matching the Rust","  `MatchedFlags` behavior.","- `eza_py/filesystem.py`: filesystem entries, Windows attributes, filtering,","  natural sorting, directory expansion, and recursion.","- `eza_py/render.py`: line, grid, long-table, and tree renderers. Renderers","  consume modeled entries and never invoke the reference binary.","- `.tura/script/differential.py`: backward-compatibility verifier. It creates","  controlled fixtures, runs the oracle and candidate independently, and","  compares all three process observables as bytes.","","## Stable behavior derived from the source","","- Option errors use status 3 (`rust-reference/src/main.rs:141`); missing input","  paths are reported while processing continues and produce status 2","  (`rust-reference/src/main.rs:272`).","- Redirected output defaults to one entry per line; a set width or `--grid`","  selects grid output (`rust-reference/src/options/view.rs:43`).","- On Windows, leading-dot and leading-underscore entries are hidden unless","  `--all`/`--almost-all` is active (`rust-reference/src/fs/dir.rs:166`).","- Sorting is stable, natural, case-insensitive by default, then optionally","  reversed and grouped by directory (`rust-reference/src/fs/filter.rs:136`).","- Tree rows are depth-first and use `├──`, `│`, and `└──` trunk state","  (`rust-reference/src/output/tree.rs:77`).","- Windows long mode renders mode, size, and selected timestamps but not Unix","  owner/group/inode/link fields (`rust-reference/src/output/table.rs:75`).","","## Entrypoint contract","","`compile.sh` is idempotent. On Windows it removes higher-priority extensionless","entrypoints and emits `executable.cmd`; on Unix-like systems it emits a valid,","executable Python launcher named `executable`. It does not compile, download,","or vendor another implementation.","","## Validation gates","","1. Python syntax compilation for every implementation and verifier module.","2. Idempotent `compile.sh` execution and direct entrypoint smoke test.","3. Focused parser and renderer unit tests.","4. Full `.tura/script/differential.py` corpus against the official binary,","   comparing status and raw stdout/stderr.","5. Independent end-to-end invocation through the generated root entrypoint.","","No passing gate is accepted as a proxy for another gate; the differential","corpus must explicitly cover each benchmark behavior area."],"path":"architect.md"}],"command":"apply_patch","command_index":0,"command_line":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: architect.md\n+# Python eza port architecture\n+\n+## Compatibility boundary\n+\n+The rebuilt command is compatible only when its process result matches the\n+official v0.23.3 Windows binary byte-for-byte: exit status, stdout, and stderr.\n+The Rust source under `rust-reference/` defines behavior; the executable named\n+by `REFERENCE_BINARY.txt` is the observable oracle.\n+\n+The benchmark scope is directory listing, long view, tree traversal, sorting,\n+hidden-file filtering, and operation with icons and colors disabled. Parser and\n+runtime errors in those paths remain part of the contract.\n+\n+## Modules\n+\n+- `eza_port.py`: process entry point and exit-code boundary.\n+- `eza_py/options.py`: eza-compatible short/long option parser and option\n+  deduction. Later occurrences override earlier occurrences, matching the Rust\n+  `MatchedFlags` behavior.\n+- `eza_py/filesystem.py`: filesystem entries, Windows attributes, filtering,\n+  natural sorting, directory expansion, and recursion.\n+- `eza_py/render.py`: line, grid, long-table, and tree renderers. Renderers\n+  consume modeled entries and never invoke the reference binary.\n+- `.tura/script/differential.py`: backward-compatibility verifier. It creates\n+  controlled fixtures, runs the oracle and candidate independently, and\n+  compares all three process observables as bytes.\n+\n+## Stable behavior derived from the source\n+\n+- Option errors use status 3 (`rust-reference/src/main.rs:141`); missing input\n+  paths are reported while processing continues and produce status 2\n+  (`rust-reference/src/main.rs:272`).\n+- Redirected output defaults to one entry per line; a set width or `--grid`\n+  selects grid output (`rust-reference/src/options/view.rs:43`).\n+- On Windows, leading-dot and leading-underscore entries are hidden unless\n+  `--all`/`--almost-all` is active (`rust-reference/src/fs/dir.rs:166`).\n+- Sorting is stable, natural, case-insensitive by default, then optionally\n+  reversed and grouped by directory (`rust-reference/src/fs/filter.rs:136`).\n+- Tree rows are depth-first and use `├──`, `│`, and `└──` trunk state\n+  (`rust-reference/src/output/tree.rs:77`).\n+- Windows long mode renders mode, size, and selected timestamps but not Unix\n+  owner/group/inode/link fields (`rust-reference/src/output/table.rs:75`).\n+\n+## Entrypoint contract\n+\n+`compile.sh` is idempotent. On Windows it removes higher-priority extensionless\n+entrypoints and emits `executable.cmd`; on Unix-like systems it emits a valid,\n+executable Python launcher named `executable`. It does not compile, download,\n+or vendor another implementation.\n+\n+## Validation gates\n+\n+1. Python syntax compilation for every implementation and verifier module.\n+2. Idempotent `compile.sh` execution and direct entrypoint smoke test.\n+3. Focused parser and renderer unit tests.\n+4. Full `.tura/script/differential.py` corpus against the official binary,\n+   comparing status and raw stdout/stderr.\n+5. Independent end-to-end invocation through the generated root entrypoint.\n+\n+No passing gate is accepted as a proxy for another gate; the differential\n+corpus must explicitly cover each benchmark